{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad","id":1126079,"title":"Werewolf Politics & Populations Circa 900AD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-07T15:47:39-07:00","id":1126079,"title":"Werewolf Politics & Populations Circa 900AD?","content":"Hi All. I'm running a M:tA game in starting in 904 AD, set in the Byzantine Empire in Constantinople (modern day Bulgaria, Greece, &amp; Turkey). My players have asked for some crossover with Werewolves &amp; Vampires. I don't know if many Werewolf books have much medieval history in them, nor do I know which Tribes/Factions would be found in those areas. Any suggestion of what books to read would be helpful, (obviously: Werewolf: the Dark Ages) as well as any suggested hooks/adventures of using Werewolves in a Mage Campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T16:06:25-07:00","id":1126089,"title":"","content":"Black Furies, Shadow Lords and Silent Striders will probably figure in the most prominently, as well the Warders (read: the ancestors of the modern day Glass Walkers) and CoGs around major urban areas. Garou that reside in Constantinople, per Werewolf: the Dark Ages, often visit other lands with works of art to try and convince more insular, misanthropic septs that humanity can do more than just soil itself and the land that it dwells upon. Furies will be pretty heavily centered on their long struggle as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T23:40:14-07:00","id":1126203,"title":"","content":"Nice, I am assuming you are doing a story involving Leo the Wise who was rumored to be a prophet and a magician.<br /> <br /> In addition to what Saur Ops Specialist said:<br /> <br /> There could be Fianna in the Galatia area of Anatolia who date from their Celtic kinfolk invading the area way back in 279 BC.<br /> <br /> Rus Norsemen had been serving as mercenaries and bodyguards of the Byzantine Emperors as early as AD 874 although they were not formally organized/recognized as the Varangian Guard until AD 988. They might indicate some presence of Get of Fenris.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs would be present in the form of House Wise Heart.<br /> <br /> Stargazers are few in number, but are associated with mountain tops. Obviously the Caucasus Mountains, the Armenian Plateau, and the Pontic Mountains are places where some might be.<br /> <br /> And being that much of the area is still wilderness, Red Talons could be present, especially in the zone between Byzantium-Arab frontier zone which greatly depopulated the area.<br /> <br /> So depending on how extensive you want to lay out the caerns and septs, you could very well have every tribe of Eurasia present albeit some in small numbers.<br /> <br /> Other than the already mentioned Werewolf: the Dark Ages, there is not much published material for the era. Tribebooks and the like gloss over the age in very brief and broad terms. And the book takes place almost three hundred years after AD 904. You would probably do better creating your own dynamics.<br /> <br /> During this time, most septs would be monotribal and this would create your Garou politics between the septs. Multi-tribal septs are extremely few, either a result of thinly populated tribes banding together for survival against the tribes in greater numbers, or as a result of a particularly powerful caern of appealing type attracting Garou of many tribes.<br /> <br /> I think for the most part, Mages and Garou of the area would ignore each other except for obvious hooks like Mages trying to steal Tass from caerns or take them over as nodes. Other possible hooks might be Garou hunting Fomori dwelling nearby to the Mages (assuming your chantry is in Constantinople or some other environment), or a common enemy to both (Nephandi who serve the Wyrm). In this era, the Black Spiral Dancers are not a significant threat having been almost wiped out centuries ago and only slowly building their numbers and finding safe places to breed and establish kinfolk. If you are interested in the rival monotheistic faiths in the Celestial Chorus, there might be conflict with the sensibilities of the Garou in the deep wilderness/rural areas.<br /> <br /> I think it is far less likely for the Garou to be interfering in the affairs of Mages, than it would be Mages (your PCs) interfering in the affairs of the Garou. So you may want to give them some kind of common enemy, but which the Mages know more about than the Garou. That way the PCs could attempt to politic with some Garou and try to win temporary allies. That might allow the PCs to befriend a small number of Garou belonging to a low powered caern, while they attempt to negotiate a greater pact/agreement with more Garou with their allies acting as intermediaries. That would allow them to interact with a large number of Garou types, meet friendly and unfriendly Garou, and have a real chance of success/failure at diplomacy based on how well the PCs do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T02:14:09-07:00","id":1126226,"title":"","content":"Red Talons and Bone Gnawers would have a lot of kin in the area. And I like to think Constantinople would be a nexus of Political struggles between Warders/Shadowlords/Children of Gaia/Silver Fangs due to what it represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T04:04:03-07:00","id":1126248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1126226#post1126226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red Talons and Bone Gnawers would have a lot of kin in the area. And I like to think Constantinople would be a nexus of Political struggles between Warders/Shadowlords/Children of Gaia/Silver Fangs due to what it represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Black Furies,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T04:14:46-07:00","id":1126252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1126248#post1126248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Black Furies,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they are greek, but I'm going with them being diffused due to their short numbers, they are not expecting to rule Constantinople, only be recognized as a power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T04:37:01-07:00","id":1126257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1126252#post1126252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they are greek, but I'm going with them being diffused due to their short numbers, they are not expecting to rule Constantinople, only be recognized as a power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not shorter than Red Talons though, at least in that area. Furies may have only girl, but they do have all breeds and Metis males, while Talons have only lupus breed and extremely low metis numbers, if any. Also the area of influence a Fury has expands to forests and cities, the only disadvsntage they may have though is that their territories tend to be claimed around ancient pagan religious regions, that may be get targeted by christian armies. While Red talons have a far greater variety of wild territory, as deep in the forests or as high on the mountains they like. but they lack urban hunting grounds, apart when taking suicide missions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:49:56-07:00","id":1126438,"title":"","content":"In a nutshell, Constantinople is likely to be one of the prize pearls of the Warders of Men, a tribe focused on interacting (covertly) with mankind, keeping an eye on what humans are up to, and playing around with their various toys (in the 10th century, that would be manuscripts, early alchemy, merchant houses, religion and philosophy). Ethnically, the Balkans (and probably parts of Asia Minor) are a strong hold of the Shadow Lords, a bunch of ruthless political provocateurs, legalistic tyrants and would be conquerers. They excel at the story of Byzantine political skullduggery the empire ended up giving it's name to. Greece and the Black Sea and Eastern Mediterranean are the homeland of the Black Furies, the all female tribe of mystical amazons who have a sacred calling to protect and defend the feminine mysteries of Nature and it's sacred places. Because they keep alive certain types of hearth wisdom and lore, they may be somewhat open to communications with any female Mage practicing the Old Ways or Spirit Talking. (However, said &quot;communications&quot; may involve a lot of attempts to correct her on her &quot;errors&quot; in belief and purpose.)<br /> <br /> You may run into others - viking berserkers, Levantine wanderers, wretched mongrel peasants, inhuman bestial savages - but the above are the main ones for crossover purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:54:09-07:00","id":1126460,"title":"","content":"Great suggestions guys, it's good to know I'm not missing too much in terms of material in the books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T19:17:37-07:00","id":1126930,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Byzantines have never been a focus for much of Werewolf, sadly. But then I've always thought that 800 AD Europe was always incredibly underrated as an RPG setting, what with two empires (Charlemagne and the Greeks), Anglo-Saxon England, the Vikings, Islamic Spain, Magyars and Bulgars, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T00:45:08-07:00","id":1128358,"title":"","content":"Yeah play Crusader Kings II as early in the timeline as you can and boom, inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T09:31:11-07:00","id":1128487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1126930#post1126930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Byzantines have never been a focus for much of Werewolf, sadly. But then I've always thought that 800 AD Europe was always incredibly underrated as an RPG setting, what with two empires (Charlemagne and the Greeks), Anglo-Saxon England, the Vikings, Islamic Spain, Magyars and Bulgars, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spain is great for werewolf, since the Islam taking over and spreading misery among the locals and making tremendous changes in the matterial and the umbra alike, new horrors from faraway lands, new banes of faith, or false faith, or even a whole new oriental maeljin cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:57:36-07:00","id":1128603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1128487#post1128487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spain is great for werewolf, since the Islam taking over and spreading misery among the locals and making tremendous changes in the matterial and the umbra alike, new horrors from faraway lands, new banes of faith, or false faith, or even a whole new oriental maeljin cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Umayyads were that bad, you'd also have to make every Church in Europe a swirling fog of chattering banes on the other side of the Umbra. They didn't exactly do astoundingly different things, when it was all said and done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T05:10:14-07:00","id":1128763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1128603#post1128603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Umayyads were that bad, you'd also have to make every Church in Europe a swirling fog of chattering banes on the other side of the Umbra. They didn't exactly do astoundingly different things, when it was all said and done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not churches, or maybe not all churches, only those that included events of violence in their peninsula and thats far away from ''all churches'', the way of how differend is a muslim invasion with a frenetic witch hunting. And yes both cases attract banes. The muslims attract the beast of war while the fanatic priests the defiler,they are just attract different aspects but still of the same beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:53:59-07:00","id":1128816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1128763#post1128763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not churches, or maybe not all churches, only those that included events of violence in their peninsula and thats far away from ''all churches'', the way of how differend is a muslim invasion with a frenetic witch hunting. And yes both cases attract banes. The muslims attract the beast of war while the fanatic priests the defiler,they are just attract different aspects but still of the same beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to make a point equating Cordoba to Constantinople because of its prosperity and success under the Ummayyads, that's one thing (and in that case, it would be bad because it's a city like Constantinople, not because of the religion of the majority of the inhabitants), but you seem to be forgetting the Crusades, the Inquisition, the heavy-handed tack taken in the Christianization of some regions of Europe, and the discrimination of the Jewish people under Christian rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T09:16:30-07:00","id":1128854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1128816#post1128816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you wanted to make a point equating Cordoba to Constantinople because of its prosperity and success under the Ummayyads, that's one thing (and in that case, it would be bad because it's a city like Constantinople, not because of the religion of the majority of the inhabitants), but you seem to be forgetting the Crusades, the Inquisition, the heavy-handed tack taken in the Christianization of some regions of Europe, and the discrimination of the Jewish people under Christian rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man this topic is not about who was the badest in th medievals, but about Garou and medieval politics.<br /> Oh and just for the mentioning the supposedly christian crusaders pillaged and destroyed the christian <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Constantinople at</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#2A2A2A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">12/04/1204, in case it escaped from your mind. I don't think they did it for religious reasons, in case you forgot mentioning it as well.<br /> <br /> The ''crusades'' have always been wyrm tainted.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T10:30:20-07:00","id":1128869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1128854#post1128854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Man this topic is not about who was the badest in th medievals, but about Garou and medieval politics.<br /> Oh and just for the mentioning the <b>supposedly christian</b> crusaders pillaged and destroyed the christian <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Constantinople at</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#2A2A2A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">12/04/1204, in case it escaped from your mind. I don't think they did it for religious reasons, in case you forgot mentioning it as well.<br /> <br /> The ''crusades'' have always been wyrm tainted.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Just say no to No True Scotsman.<br /> <br /> As for the Werewolf details, you were the first one to make a suggestion that had a weird side deviation into Garou somehow having more of a problem with Islam than with Christianity. I really don't think that they would. They have a purpose that's at odds with pretty much every human religion and belief system, since said belief systems tend to start with some form of professed importance of humanity. And, on the flipside, the time period mentioned in the OP is roughly two centuries after Spain became a part of the Umayyads, so the Christians are going to be the invading forces; before that, Hispania was the domain of the Visigoths, after being part of Rome, which means that there were banes aplenty there to begin with, as Rome wasn't clean by a long shot and its territories, likewise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T14:47:35-07:00","id":1128967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1128869#post1128869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Garou somehow having more of a problem with Islam than with Christianity. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Never said that, plus I have already covered that part to what equals what.<br /> So lets keep in topic on. Shall we ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T17:54:32-07:00","id":1129051,"title":"","content":"On topic, in Byzantium around AD 900, the First Crusade was 200 years in the future, and the political conflicts for Constantinople would have come from Slavs (and/or Vikings) to the North and from Arabs to the South. I'm not sure how much interest the various Garou tribes would have taken in these human wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T19:31:38-07:00","id":1129087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1129051#post1129051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On topic, in Byzantium around AD 900, the First Crusade was 200 years in the future, and the political conflicts for Constantinople would have come from Slavs (and/or Vikings) to the North and from Arabs to the South. I'm not sure how much interest the various Garou tribes would have taken in these human wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first Silver Fangs tribebook also notes some influence in Byzantium, but mostly concentrates on their tribal quest during that time to free the Children of Karnak, so it appears that they probably didn't pay enough attention. This is in contrast to the Western Roman Empire, where the local ruling house of Fangs, which was ousted from influence by other supernatural nastiness and ended up committing suicide during the Renaissance after hanging on for a number of centuries. Apparently, they suffered Harano, one and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T07:15:30-07:00","id":1129212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126079-werewolf-politics-populations-circa-900ad?p=1129051#post1129051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On topic, in Byzantium around AD 900, the First Crusade was 200 years in the future, and the political conflicts for Constantinople would have come from Slavs (and/or Vikings) to the North and from Arabs to the South. I'm not sure how much interest the various Garou tribes would have taken in these human wars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Arabs coul include Silent strider kinfolk and the Striders might take action to protect them if their kin traveled in Vyzantean ground, the other side of the conflict might be an alliance betweeen Shadow Lords and Silverfangs, yup an alliance in that era might be highly possible if only temporary, in order to protect their turf from northern and southern intruders, plus players will get jawdroped when hearing about that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> Pagan Fenrir and ''muslim'' Striders vs ''christian'' balkan tribes might be an intriguing scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:20:30-07:00","id":1129388,"title":"","content":"Silent Striders (and any other homed-born Garou in the 9th century Eastern Mediterranean) would be just as likely to be Coptic, Syriac or Armenian Orthodox as they are Muslim. Although, from the Garou point of view, both Christianity and Islam are seen as the work of the Patriarch Incarna of the Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jp